{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23795 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (-)-Tanegol and SK-VLB, mediated through Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, with (-)-Tanegol directly targeting this enzyme, which in turn is the target of 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether and 5-Fluorouracil1-acetic acid hydrazide, all of which have a known effect on SK-VLB. The scores for these relationships are consistent, indicating a plausible mechanistic link. The core mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which may modulate cellular signaling pathways critical for SK-VLB function. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway suggests a potential for broader therapeutic application, though further validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between (-)-Tanegol and SK-VLB. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway involving enzyme inhibition, but the exact mode of action and the role of the intermediate targets remain to be fully elucidated.",
